Examples for the ILVES bond/angle constraint solver.

The ILVES solver comes in two variants:

  * fix ilves/global -- gathers the complete bond/angle topology onto
    every MPI rank at init.  Per-rank memory scales with the total
    system size, but the variant handles arbitrarily large connected
    constraint clusters (e.g. all C-C backbone bonds of a long polymer
    chain in a single cluster).

  * fix ilves/local  -- builds the constraint list from each rank's
    own bond/angle storage only; no global topology gather, no
    natoms-sized cluster table.  Every constraint cluster must fit
    within a single subdomain plus the communication cutoff, and the
    cluster topology must be star-shaped (one central atom with k
    leaves) or a 1+1 pair.  Requires "newton off bond".  Suitable for
    water HOH constraints, methyl / methane groups, isolated C-H bonds
    -- the common ILVES use cases.

Both variants accept the same selectors (b/a/t/m) and keywords
(kbond, store, variant) as fix shake.  So the fix shake usage:

    fix cstr all shake 1.0e-4 25 0 b 4 6 8 10 12 14 18 a 31

becomes either:

    fix cstr all ilves/global 1.0e-4 25 0 b 4 6 8 10 12 14 18 a 31
    fix cstr all ilves/local  1.0e-4 25 0 b 4 6 8 10 12 14 18 a 31

Two solver variants are available via the *variant* keyword:
  * variant = ilvesf (default): symmetric Jacobian using r_k.r_l in
    off-diagonals; solved with in-place Cholesky.
  * variant = ilves : the structurally-symmetric exact Newton
    Jacobian using s_k.r_l in off-diagonals; solved with LU.

Both converge to the exact solution of the constraint equations.

Example input files:
  in.peptide-ilves    -- peptide + water with ilves/global, exact-Newton variant
  in.peptide-ilvesf   -- peptide + water with ilves/global, symmetric variant
  in.peptide-local    -- peptide + water with ilves/local (newton off bond)
  in.peptide-mix      -- peptide groups via ilves/global, water via fix shake
  in.peptide-allbonds -- ilves/global constraining ALL bonds, demonstrating
                         arbitrarily-large cluster support (not feasible with
                         ilves/local, since the backbone forms a multi-hop chain)
  in.peptide-shake    -- baseline using fix shake for comparison
  in.peptide-rattle   -- baseline using fix rattle for comparison
